        "### Reversible Cholesterol-Receptor Binding Kinetics\n",
        "\n",
        "In physiology, the reversible binding of a ligand (Cholesterol, $L$) to a receptor ($R$) to form a ligand-receptor complex ($LR$) is represented by the chemical equation:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$L + R \\underset{k_{\\text{off}}}{\\overset{k_{\\text{on}}}{\\rightleftharpoons}} LR$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Where:\n",
        "* $[L]$ is the concentration of free cholesterol.\n",
        "* $[R]$ is the concentration of free receptors.\n",
        "* $[LR]$ is the concentration of the cholesterol-receptor complex.\n",
        "* $k_{\\text{on}}$ (or $k_f$) is the association (forward) rate constant.\n",
        "* $k_{\\text{off}}$ (or $k_r$) is the dissociation (reverse) rate constant.\n",
        "\n",
        "#### System of Ordinary Differential Equations (ODEs)\n",
        "\n",
        "Assuming a closed system, the rate of change of each component over time can be described by the following system of differential equations:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\frac{d[LR]}{dt} = k_{\\text{on}}[L][R] - k_{\\text{off}}[LR]$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\frac{d[L]}{dt} = -k_{\\text{on}}[L][R] + k_{\\text{off}}[LR]$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\frac{d[R]}{dt} = -k_{\\text{on}}[L][R] + k_{\\text{off}}[LR]$$"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
