        "### Steady-State Receptor Occupancy vs. Free Ligand Concentration\n",
        "\n",
        "At steady state, the fractional occupancy ($\\theta$) is defined as the ratio of bound receptors to total receptors:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\theta = \\frac{[LR]}{[R]_{\\text{total}}} = \\frac{[L]}{[L] + K_d}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Where $K_d$ is the equilibrium dissociation constant ($K_d = k_{\\text{off}} / k_{\\text{on}}$).\n",
        "\n",
        "* When $[L] = K_d$, exactly $50\\%$ of the receptors are occupied ($\\theta = 0.5$).\n",
        "* When $[L] \\gg K_d$, occupancy approaches $100\\%$ (saturation)."
      ]
    },
